  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and preferring the more right-skewed lottery, which in this case is Lottery B (67% vs. 66% on 0 Euros). However, the individual does not mention skewness, probability distribution shape, or the relative concentration of probability on unfavorable outcomes. Instead, their justification centers on the small probability difference (1%) and the 100 Euro payoff difference, suggesting a focus on expected value or direct trade-off between probability and payoff. The reasoning is based on marginal differences in probability and value, not on the structural property of skewness. Therefore, the decision reason is not reflected in the individual’s deliberation process. The individual did not use the skewness-based reason to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
